    - wrap.py
        - Numerous bugs in code
        - A common need is to dedent help text.  Add a function wrapit(s) that takes a
          string s and provides a minilanguage:
            - '.out expr' turns output on & off (on & off as words work too)
                - '.out off' is good for providing documentation in the string
            - '.on expr' turns formatting on
            - '.off expr' turns it off (i.e., output things verbatim)
            - '.indent n' for n integer >= 0
            - '.save varname' saves the state
            - '.restore varname' restores the state
            - '.psep value' paragraph separator (\n\n is default)
            - Default behavior is to first remove common leading whitespace from all
              lines, just as dedent() does.  An empty newline will match the indentation
              of the previous or following lines.
        - Question:  can the heavy lifting be done adequately with the textwrap
          module?

